  "content": {
    "id": "p30-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=x^2+2x+10$ and $g(x)=\\log_3x$. Find the range of the function $g\\circ f$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$[2,\\infty)$.\n\nThe inner function has minimum $9$, and $\\log_3x$ is increasing.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=x^2+2x+10\\\\f(x)&=(x+1)^2+9\\end{align*}$$\nThus $f(x)\\ge9$, with equality at $x=-1$. Since $\\log_3x$ is increasing,\n$$\\begin{align*}(g\\circ f)(x)&=\\log_3\\bigl((x+1)^2+9\\bigr)\\\\(g\\circ f)(x)&\\ge\\log_3 9\\\\(g\\circ f)(x)&\\ge2\\end{align*}$$\nEvery value at least $2$ is attained, so the range is $[2,\\infty)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
  },
